	"descriptionMarkdown": "Train-based logistics can end up being a real headache if not properly set up for scaling.  After dealing with the hassle with partial solutions for **FAR** too long, I buckled down to combine DocJade's interrupt-based train route scheduling with a solid, indefinitely stackable depot and loading/unloading stations that broadcast how many full train loads they have/need, incorporating limits and priorities based on buffer contents to make sure that resources can continue to flow smoothly, all the way up to the megabase stage.\n\nv1.0.0/2026/KeithFromCanada",
